# FortMesa Saferoom VSIX packaging exclusions.
#
# The packaged .vsix needs the bundled extension host code AND the bundled
# CLI/proxy (dist-ext/**, produced by `yarn build:ext` + `yarn build:cli`)
# plus `launch-mcp.sh` (W1 / T020: the extension spawns the proxy from its
# OWN install path now, independent of any open workspace folder — see
# extension.ts's `resolveServerSpec`), plus manifest/doc files that vsce
# reads directly (package.json, README.md) and the activity-bar icon it
# references. Everything else here is CLI/extension SOURCE (bundled, not
# needed raw), the PnP toolchain (the bundled CLI has no runtime dependency
# on it — see `build:cli`'s doc comment), the tsc CLI build output (a
# separate, unbundled artifact for repo/dev use only), or workspace/agent
# tooling that has no business in a sideloadable extension package.

# Source (bundled into dist-ext/extension.cjs by esbuild — not needed raw)
src/**
scripts/**

# CLI build output (separate artifact — dist/local-mcp/cli.js; the VSIX
# ships dist-ext/**, not dist/**)
dist/**

# Yarn PnP toolchain (build-time only; defensively exclude node_modules in
# case the linker is ever switched)
.yarn/**
.yarnrc.yml
.pnp.cjs
.pnp.loader.mjs
node_modules/**
yarn.lock

# Tests / fixtures
test/**
**/__tests__/**
**/*.test.mjs
**/*.test.ts

# Workspace/agent tooling and planning docs — not extension-relevant
.agent/**
.git/**
.github/**
.husky/**

# Build/lint/format config — irrelevant to the packaged extension
tsconfig.json
eslint.config.mjs
.prettierrc
.prettierignore
.gitignore

# npm-tarball packing rules — governs the `fmmcp-local` npm distribution only,
# has no meaning inside a VSIX. Must be listed here: vsce has no default
# ignore for it, so without this line it ships inside the extension (caught by
# a before/after VSIX content diff — it added a 15th file to the package).
.npmignore

# CI definition — build-time only, nothing to do with the packaged extension.
# Same story as .npmignore: vsce has no default ignore for it and it leaked
# into the VSIX until it was listed here.
bitbucket-pipelines.yml

# The npm tarball and the MCP Bundle, both written into the repo root
# alongside the .vsix by the pipeline's package step. vsce already excludes
# *.vsix from its own output by default, but neither of these — without them
# the CLI tarball and the .mcpb would be embedded inside the extension.
*.tgz
*.mcpb

# Misc repo docs not part of the VSIX-facing documentation surface
CHANGELOG.md
SPECS.md
SECURITY.md
DISTRIBUTION.md
ERRATA.md
TODOS.md
AGENTS.md
BURNDOWN-ARCHIVE.md
BURNDOWN-DECISIONS.md
BURNDOWN-INBOX.md
BURNDOWN-OPEN.md

# LICENSE, NOTICE and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md are DELIBERATELY NOT listed
# above — vsce includes any file it isn't told to exclude, so these three
# ship at the extension package root by default. Called out here (as a
# non-match) because vsce does NOT include NOTICE by default the way it
# includes LICENSE*, and OpenVSX's license detection reads package.json's
# "license" field plus these files at the package root — do not add any
# of the three to this ignore list.
#
# CONTRIBUTING.md needs the opposite treatment: vsce's built-in
# `defaultIgnore` list excludes CONTRIBUTING.md unconditionally (it assumes
# a repo-only doc), and that default applies even though nothing above
# names the file — the negation below is required to force it back in.
!CONTRIBUTING.md

# Editor/OS cruft
**/.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
